course: dictionary
lesson: 3001
title: Duplicate: an exact copy
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. «Dad had a duplicate key cut so I could get in after school.» The word copy and the key being cut tell you that duplicate means an exact copy of something.
explain: As a verb, to duplicate means to make an exact copy, or to do something again that was already done. «Two copies of the same script run twice, so a coin can add 2 instead of 1; duplicate code is a common bug after copy and paste.» Here the clues are copies, run twice and copy and paste, so duplicate code means the same code written out again by mistake.
explain: Always check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence. Does "an exact copy of the code" make sense here? Yes, so you have found the right meaning. If you are still unsure, look at the words around it first, then use a dictionary.
fact: Duplicate means an exact copy of something.
fact: Duplicate can be a noun («a duplicate key»), a verb («to duplicate a file») or an adjective («duplicate copies»).
fact: «In duplicate» means in two copies, as in «Please sign the form in duplicate.»
fact: In card collecting, duplicates are spare copies of cards you already have, and they are often swapped with friends.
fact: In computing and data work, duplicates are repeated items that should be removed, so the list is correct.
exercise: «Dad had a duplicate key cut so I could get in after school.» What is a duplicate key? | A key for a different door | A broken key that will not turn | A key made of gold | *An exact copy of a key
exercise: «Two copies of the same script run twice, so a coin can add 2 instead of 1.» What goes wrong here? | *The same code runs twice, so the result is doubled | The script runs too slowly to read | The coin is lost | The copies are painted different colours
exercise: In card collecting, what are duplicates? | Cards kept in a special box | *Spare copies of cards you already have | Cards that are bent or torn | Cards you have lost
test: Miss Lee said, «We will duplicate the experiment to check the results.» What does duplicate mean here? | To throw the results away | *To do the experiment again | To make the experiment longer | To hide the answers
test: «Please sign the form in duplicate.» What does in duplicate mean? | *In two copies | Without a name | In a hurry | In red ink
exam: «The computer found duplicates in the list, so it removed the repeated names.» What were the duplicates? | Names that were missing | Names written in capital letters | New names added to the list | *Repeated items that were the same
